What carries over from the original: the shape of the integration (auto-recall
before the prompt is built, non-blocking auto-capture after a turn, and the
four model-callable tools memory_search/list/store/forget, here renamed
memory_recall/list/store/forget).

What I changed, so that this is a modified work:
  - ported from the removed provider API (registerMemoryProvider, after_turn,
    appendSystem) to OpenClaw 2026.11.10 (registerMemoryCapability,
    before_prompt_build appendSystemContext, agent_end);
  - talks to CortexDB through Teeny's own client (core/src/memory/cortex.ts),
    self-hosted and loopback or https only, instead of the cortexdbai SDK and
    its cloud default;
  - memory_forget deletes only the learnings that match its query, needs a
    reason, and refuses when more than 5 match; the original ignored the query
    and wiped the whole scope;
  - capture is limited to an agent allowlist, size-capped and screened.
